* LM358 behavioural macromodel - one op-amp section
*
* Pins: IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT   (same order as TI/ON Semi PSpice models,
*                              so an official model can be dropped in)
*
* Written for this project (not a vendor model). It reproduces the
* datasheet limits that matter for the analog front end:
*   - open-loop gain AOL, gain-bandwidth GBW, slew rate SR
*   - input offset VOS and input bias current IB (PNP input: flows out of pins)
*   - output swing: ~VEE (light load) up to VCC - VHR
*   - class-B output stage with a VXO dead band and a 50 uA internal sink,
*     so crossover distortion appears when the load needs more than ISINK
* Not modelled: input common-mode limit (VCC - 1.5 V), noise, PSRR/CMRR,
* temperature drift, second poles.
*
* Typical LM358 values (5 V supply, 25 C): AOL 100 V/mV, GBW 0.7 MHz,
* SR 0.3 V/us, VOS 2 mV typ (7 mV max), IB 45 nA (250 nA max).

.subckt LM358B inp inn vcc vee out VOS=2m IB=45n AOL=100k GBW=0.7Meg SR=0.3Meg ISINK=50u VXO=0.6 VHR=1.5
.param CC=1n
.param GM={2*pi*GBW*CC}
.param IMAX={SR*CC}
.param RO={AOL/GM}

* supply current (both sections of the package draw ~0.7 mA)
Iq vcc vee 350u

* input offset and bias currents
Vos inp inpo {VOS}
Ibp vcc inp {IB}
Ibn vcc inn {IB}

* mid-supply reference for the integrator
Bmid mid 0 V=(V(vcc)+V(vee))/2

* transconductance with slew limit, integrating into CC (dominant pole)
Bgm 0 x I={IMAX}*tanh({GM}*(V(inpo)-V(inn))/{IMAX})
Cc x mid {CC}
Ro x mid {RO}

* clamp the integrator node so the output stops at VEE / VCC-VHR
* and recovers from saturation without wind-up
Vhi xhi vcc {-VHR+0.6}
Dhi x xhi DCLMP
Dlo vee x DCLMP

* class-B output stage
*   source path: NPN follower, conducts when out < x - 0.6
*   sink path:   PNP, conducts when out > x - 1.2 + VXO
*   between the two (width VXO) only the 50 uA sink is active
Ey y 0 x 0 1
Dsrc y out DOUT
Byn yn 0 V=V(x)+{VXO}-1.2
Dsnk out yn DOUT
Isnk out vee {ISINK}

.model DCLMP D(IS=1e-14 N=0.05)
.model DOUT D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=20)
.ends LM358B
